    {
      "slug": "baklava-term",
      "term": "Baklava",
      "definition": "A rich pastry of layered filo and nuts soaked in honey or sugar syrup, found across Turkey, Greece and the Middle East."
    }
  ],
  "techniqueSlugs": [],
  "criticalTechniques": [],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe serves 12 and takes 45 minutes to prepare and 40 minutes to cook. Sheets of filo pastry are layered with crushed pistachios and walnuts, brushed generously with clarified butter at every layer, baked until golden and then immediately soaked in a fragrant honey and rose water syrup."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tip: the syrup must go onto the baklava the moment it comes out of the oven. Hot pastry absorbs cold syrup perfectly. If you add cold syrup to cold baklava, it pools on top rather than soaking in."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
